---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Tracking competency growth — apprenti.dev Docs">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">
                Tracking competency growth
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Competencies in apprenti.dev are not a self-rated
                    progress bar. They exist to answer one question
                    defensibly: <em
                        >what can this apprentice actually do, and what's the
                        evidence?</em
                    >
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Levels</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Every competency has five levels:
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Foundation
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Apprentice
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Practitioner
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Journeyman
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Mastery Evidence
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Where evidence comes from
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Only <strong>approved</strong> tasks and submissions
                    count as evidence toward a competency. Work that's still
                    in progress, submitted-but-not-yet-reviewed, or sent
                    back for revision does not contribute — an apprentice
                    cannot self-award progress, and neither can an
                    unreviewed submission.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    What you can do as a mentor
                </h2>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Open the
                        evidence list behind any competency and trace every
                        claim back to a specific approved task
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Assign or
                        change a competency level yourself, with the change
                        recorded durably (and its history preserved) in Git
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Review an
                        AI-suggested level if one is offered — it is always
                        clearly labeled non-authoritative and requires your
                        approval before it means anything
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Use gap
                        detection and suggested next tasks to steer what an
                        apprentice should work on next
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    The guarantee
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Every competency claim a mentor or apprentice can see
                    must trace back to approved evidence that a mentor can
                    open and inspect. If it can't, it isn't real progress
                    yet — it's a suggestion.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline"
                >← All Docs</a
            >
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to apprenti.dev</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
